    title "Top 20 Transgender Films | Style is Substance"
    description "In this video, we will take a look at what I personally consider to be the best transgender films. For this list, I will be exploring my favorite films that prominently feature transgender or gender-questioning characters and/or documentary subjects. &#10;&#10;Feel free to SUBSCRIBE.&#10;&#11088; Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/styleissubstance&#10;&#11088;Twitter: https://twitter.com/SubstanceIs&#10;&#11088; Letterboxd: https://letterboxd.com/Jay96/&#10;&#11088; e-mail: styleissubstance1@gmail.com&#10;&#10;Chapters:&#10;0:00:00 &#8212; Intro&#10;0:01:31 &#8212; 22. WOMEN IN REVOLT (1971, Paul Morrissey)&#10;0:05:55 &#8212; 21. GLEN OR GLENDA (1953, Edward D. Wood Jr.)&#10;0:10:37 &#8212; 20. MY LIFE IN PINK (1997, Alain Berliner)&#10;0:13:39 &#8212; 19. THE LAW OF DESIRE (1987, Pedro Almod&#243;var)&#10;0:17:07 &#8212; 18. SE&#209;ORITA (2011, Isabel Sandoval)&#10;0:20:29 &#8212; 17. I DON'T KNOW (1971, Penelope Spheeris)&#10;0:22:56 &#8212; 16. A FANTASTIC WOMAN (2017, Sebasti&#225;n Lelio)&#10;0:25:34 &#8212; 15. THE CRYING GAME (1992, Neil Jordan)&#10;0:29:13 &#8212; 14. BAD EDUCATION (2004, Pedro Almod&#243;var)&#10;0:32:26 &#8212; 13. TOMBOY (2011, C&#233;line Sciamma)&#10;0:34:36 &#8212; 12. JURASSIC PARK (1993, Steven Spielberg)&#10;0:38:20 &#8212; 11. ALL ABOUT MY MOTHER (1999, Pedro Almod&#243;var)&#10;0:41:47 &#8212; 10. SHINJUKU BOYS (1995, Kim Longinotto and Jano Williams)&#10;0:45:42 &#8212; 09. LET THE RIGHT ONE IN (2008, Thomas Alfredson)&#10;0:48:48 &#8212; 08. PARIS IS BURNING (1990, Jennie Livingston)&#10;0:52:07 &#8212; 07. LINGUA FRANCA (2019, Isabel Sandoval)&#10;0:55:36 &#8212; 06. BOYS DON'T CRY (1999, Kimberly Peirce)&#10;0:59:19 &#8212; 05. DOG DAY AFTERNOON (1975, Sidney Lumet)&#10;1:04:05 &#8212; 04. THE SILENCE OF THE LAMBS (1991, Jonathan Demme)&#10;1:09:17 &#8212; 03. IN A YEAR OF 13 MOONS (1978, Rainer Werner Fassbinder)&#10;1:13:16 &#8212; 02. HEDWIG AND THE ANGRY INCH (2001, John Cameron Mitchell)&#10;1:19:04 &#821