  node [
    id 257
    label "7AS5RQx0CK0"
    step 0
    date "2022-07-13T14:30:03Z"
    title "Transgender Athlete Policies Are About To Change Sports FOREVER.. Heres Why"
    description "Transgender Athlete Policies Are About To Change Sports FOREVER.. Here's Why&#10;&#10;Welcome back to Athlete District, today on the channel we are going to talk about the AOC president Ian Chesterman says transgender athlete policies are up to individual sports + other related news. The Australian Olympic Committee (AOC) says it will leave policies around transgender athletes up to individual sports, in line with the International Olympic Committee's (IOC) guidelines. Transgender women's futures in elite sports has once again made headlines after FINA, swimming's world governing body, earlier this week voted to effectively ban transgender swimmers from elite women's competitions. Swimming is the first Olympic sport to adopt such an edict and it has sparked a chain reaction elsewhere.&#10;&#10;International Rugby League has excluded transgender athletes from sanctioned international matches, including this year's Rugby League Women's World Cup in England. FIFA, World Athletics and the World Netball Federation are all reviewing their respective policies. The IOC last year revised its guidelines on inclusion, with a new framework advising that athletes should not be excluded from competition on the grounds of &#34;perceived&#34; unfair advantage, but has ultimately left it up to sports federations to decide the rules. The AOC will follow the global Olympic body's lead. &#34;The thing we constantly need to focus on is the fact that sport needs to be inclusive,&#34; Chesterman said. &#34;We need to create opportunities for every young Australian and, particularly, if you come from a marginalised group. We need to be encouraging you to be using sport as part of your development and your growth.&#8221; However, while some high-profile sports such as swimming and rugby league have enacted blanket bans, other sports around the world are moving in the opposite direction. On Friday, Germany's football federation announced that transgender, intersex and non-binary athletes at youth, futsal and amateur level would be allowed to decide for themselves in which competitions they participate.&#10;&#10;#TransgenderAthletePolicies  #AOC  #SportsRules&#10;&#10;Related Videos:&#10;&#10;Trans Athletes in Sports&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wCZA7blfPn8&#10;&#10;Kiwi transgender athlete slams world swimming's so-called gender inclusion policy&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b40Gkab_038&#10;&#10;Should &#8220;Transgender Women&#8221; Be Allowed to Compete in Women&#8217;s Sports?&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7D6btYpcgU0"
    channeltitle "Athlete District"
